{"slug":"wildcard-pattern-match","title":"Does the Pattern With Wildcards Match the Text?","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":751,"tags":["dp","string","pattern-matching","wildcard"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A table over the prefixes of the text and of the pattern: a star can eat nothing or one more letter","body":["A pattern may contain ordinary letters, the character `?` (matches **any one** letter) and the character `*` (matches **any sequence of letters, also an empty one**). The pattern must match the **whole** text. For the text `adceb` and the pattern `*a*b` the answer is yes (`*` = empty, `a`, `*` = `dce`, `b`). For `acdcb` and `a*c?b` it is no.","Let `ok(i, j)` be true if the first `i` letters of the text match the first `j` characters of the pattern. The empty text matches the empty pattern, and also a pattern made only of stars. Look at the last pattern character `p[j]`. If it is a **letter or `?`**, it must match exactly one text letter `t[i]` (equal, or any for `?`): `ok(i, j) = ok(i - 1, j - 1)`. If it is a **`*`**, it either matches nothing, `ok(i, j - 1)`, or it eats one more letter of the text and may continue to be used, `ok(i - 1, j)`: **`ok(i, j) = ok(i, j - 1) or ok(i - 1, j)`**.",{"code":"prev = [True] + [False] * m                     # i = 0: the empty text\nfor j in range(1, m + 1):\n    prev[j] = prev[j - 1] and p[j - 1] == \"*\"\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    cur = [False] * (m + 1)\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        c = p[j - 1]\n        if c == \"*\":\n            cur[j] = cur[j - 1] or prev[j]\n        elif c == \"?\" or c == t[i - 1]:\n            cur[j] = prev[j - 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(\"yes\" if prev[m] else \"no\")"},"The two cases of the star are the whole difficulty. A greedy search that tries to guess how much the star should eat can take exponential time in the worst case; the table is O(n * m) = one million steps and, with two rows, O(m) memory."]},"statement":["A text `t` and a pattern `p` are given. In the pattern, `?` matches any single letter and `*` matches any sequence of letters (possibly empty); every other character matches itself. Print `yes` if the pattern matches the whole text, otherwise `no`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the text `t` (lowercase letters).","The second line has the pattern `p` (lowercase letters, `?` and `*`)."],"outputFormat":["Print `yes` or `no`."],"constraints":["1 <= length of t <= 1000","1 <= length of p <= 1000"],"examples":[{"input":"adceb\n*a*b\n","output":"yes\n","note":"The first star is empty, the second star is dce: yes."},{"input":"acdcb\na*c?b\n","output":"no\n","note":"After a*c there must be exactly one letter before b, but there are two options that fail: no."}],"hints":["Let ok(i, j) be true if the first i letters of the text match the first j characters of the pattern.","A letter or ? needs ok(i - 1, j - 1) and a matching letter.","A star gives ok(i, j - 1) (empty) or ok(i - 1, j) (eats one more letter)."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nt = input().strip()\np = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String t = next();\n        String p = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["ok(i, j) tells whether the first i letters of the text match the first j characters of the pattern: a letter or ? needs ok(i - 1, j - 1) and a matching letter, a star gives ok(i, j - 1) or ok(i - 1, j). Two rows are kept; the answer is ok(n, m)."],"complexity":"Time O(n * m), space O(m).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nt = input().strip()\np = input().strip()\n\nn = len(t)\nm = len(p)\nprev = [True] + [False] * m\nfor j in range(1, m + 1):\n    prev[j] = prev[j - 1] and p[j - 1] == \"*\"\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    cur = [False] * (m + 1)\n    ti = t[i - 1]\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        c = p[j - 1]\n        if c == \"*\":\n            cur[j] = cur[j - 1] or prev[j]\n        elif c == \"?\" or c == ti:\n            cur[j] = prev[j - 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(\"yes\" if prev[m] else \"no\")\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n\n    int n = (int)t.size(), m = (int)p.size();\n    vector<char> prev(m + 1, 0), cur(m + 1, 0);\n    prev[0] = 1;\n    for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) prev[j] = prev[j - 1] && p[j - 1] == '*';\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        cur[0] = 0;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n            char c = p[j - 1];\n            if (c == '*') cur[j] = cur[j - 1] || prev[j];\n            else if (c == '?' || c == t[i - 1]) cur[j] = prev[j - 1];\n            else cur[j] = 0;\n        }\n        swap(prev, cur);\n    }\n    cout << (prev[m] ? \"yes\" : \"no\") << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String t = next();\n        String p = next();\n\n        int n = t.length(), m = p.length();\n        boolean[] prev = new boolean[m + 1];\n        boolean[] cur = new boolean[m + 1];\n        prev[0] = true;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) prev[j] = prev[j - 1] && p.charAt(j - 1) == '*';\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            cur[0] = false;\n            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n                char c = p.charAt(j - 1);\n                if (c == '*') cur[j] = cur[j - 1] || prev[j];\n                else if (c == '?' || c == t.charAt(i - 1)) cur[j] = prev[j - 1];\n                else cur[j] = false;\n            }\n            boolean[] swap = prev;\n            prev = cur;\n            cur = swap;\n        }\n        System.out.println(prev[m] ? \"yes\" : \"no\");\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"adceb\n*a*b\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"acdcb\na*c?b\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"a\n*\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"a\n?\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"ab\n?\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"abc\nabd\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"aaabbbbaaabbbbbaabaa\nbbbababb**\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"babbbababababbabaaabaababaaaaaaababaaaabababbbbbbbaabbabababbaabaaabaaabaaaabbabbaabbabbbaaaabaaabba\nbbbabbbb*b*a?b*ababaab*?bbbb?abba*aaaabb????*a*aba\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\nabbaba*babaaba?bbb?abbabaabbababa?bbbba*?aababaaaab?aaaabbaaabababbaababbb?aabbbabbb?ba*abbabba?aabb\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\nbbbbaababbbaaabbbababbaaaabababbaaabaaaabbabbabbbabaaaabaaababbbabaabbabbbbbbaabaaba?bbbabbaaaaba?baaabaaabbabaabaaababbababbbaabbabbbaaaaaababaaaaaabaaabbabbbabbbbababbab?aabbbbbbbaaabaabbabbbbabbaaabbaaaaaaababbaababbbaaaabbabbabaabababaabbbbbabaaaaaabbbabaaabababbbaaaa?aaabaababbbabaababbbbabbaaabaaabaaabaab*bababbbaabaaaaababbbabaaaaabbaaabbaaabaabbaaa?ababaaaaaabbaabbabbbababaabbbababbaaaaaaabbbbabbbaabaaabbbbb?aababaabbbbabbabaabaaaabbaaaabbbbabbaabababbb?bbabaabaaabbababbbaaababbabbabaaabbbbaaabaaab*babbbaaababbaaabbaa*baabaaabaabbabaaaaaababbbbabaabaabbabbabaaaaaabbaa*aabaaabbabbabbbaaaaaaaabbababaaaabbaabbaabaababb*bbabababaaaaaaab?abbaabbabbabbbbbbabaabbaabbbbba*baababbbabaabbababbabbabaababbbbaaabbbabbbbbbaaabbbabbbabbbabaaaab*abaaaaabbbbaabaababababaaaaabbaaababbabbbaabbabbaaaabaaabaabbaabbabbaaabbabbaabbababaabbaaabababbaaabbbaabbbbbbabbaaabaabbbbabaababba*b?aaaabbababbbaaabbbbaa*aa?baabbbbabbbbbbaaabbaaabbbbbaaaaababbabbaabbabbabbaaababaaaababbbbbabaaaa*aabbaabbabbaab?aab\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\nbabccbcbacc?bacbbbabbbbcbacbcccabcbaacaacabbccccaacbccab*bccccccbcccaaabacacbb?accaa?baaa?bcabcaaabbbcca*acaa?baca*bcbcccbbaa?abacbccabaaaaaac?aabbcbccabbbbcbbcc*bcbbc?aaca?cccacccabaa*aaca?ccc?abcccccabbac?cbbca?babc*cbbbcacbbcccbbcbcbcbbaa*acacbabc??*?bbac?caaccbcbabbabbacbccbcaaacabbcabbabbbaaaa?\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\n*aaaaaa**aaaaaaaa**a***a**a**********a****aa**aaaa***a*a**a*aaaaaa**aa*a*a**aa***aa*a***a**a*a*a***a*aa*aaaaaa*a*****a*aa*a**a*aaa*aaa****aa***a*aaa*a**a*aaa*aaa*a*a*aa*a**a******aa**aaa**aa*a*aa*a*aaaaaa**a*aaa*aaa****aa*a*a*aa*aa**aaa**aaaaa********aa*aa*a**aaa*a*a**a******a****aa**a**aaa*aaa*aa***a*aa***a***aaa*aaaaaaa**a***aa*a*aa**a***aa***a*a***a*a********aaa**a*aaaaaa*a*aa***aa*****aaaaaa*aaa***a**a*aaa*a*aa**aa*a*a*a*aa*aa**aaaaaaaa*aa*aa***a*aaaaa*******aaaa*a*a*aa*a*aaaaa**aa***aaa*aaa**a****a*a*a**a****a*aaaa*aa***a**aa*a******a******aa*a*aa******aaaaa*a***aaaa*aa*a****a*a**aa*a*a***a*a*aaa**a**a**aa**a***aaaaaa**aa*aa**a*a*aa*aa*a**aaaa**a*aaa**aaaaaaa*aa*a***aaaa*aa***************aaa***aa**aaaaaaaaaaaaa**a*****aa*aa*aaa*aa***aaa***aa*****aaaaaa*aaaa*aaaa*aa*aaaa*******a*aa*******aa**aa**a**a*a*aa*a*a*a*aaa**aaa****a*a*a***aaa**aaa**a*aa**a*aaa*aa*a*a*aa***a****aaa*aaa*****aa**a***aaa**aa*aa*aa*a**aa*a***aa*a**a*a**a***aa**aa**aaaaaa****a**a**